# local tooling / editor. `.claude/` is ignored except the four files every worktree
# needs: the three that carry the worktree-per-change rule, and the launch config the
# preview starts the static server from. A worktree only gets a file if git puts it
# there, so anything ignored here is missing from the tree every change is made in.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/worktree-per-change.json
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/launch.json
.openai/
.agents/
.codex/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log

# node / vercel local artifacts (not used, kept out just in case)
node_modules/
.vercel/
dist/

# where design/tools/check-capture-contract.py stages the profile repo's capture
# script and the screenshots it takes. It lives beside design/tools/node_modules
# because ESM resolves `playwright` from the running script's own directory, so
# the fetched script has to sit under the install rather than anywhere tidier.
# Nothing in here is committed — the capture is fetched fresh every run, on
# purpose, so a vendored copy cannot drift against a repo we do not own.
design/tools/.capture-contract/

# python bytecode — design/og/build-og.py is the only Python here
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# full-resolution photo originals (~250MB) — the site uses the optimised copies
# in img/. Kept local to keep the repo lean and Vercel deploys fast. Regenerate
# img/ from these with the Pillow step in README.md.
photos/

# camera raws, wherever they are dropped. Same reasoning as photos/ — a single
# RW2 off the GX80 is ~19MB — but by extension, because the one the corner plate
# is built from is handed to design/plate/build-plate.py by path and so tends to
# sit wherever it was unpacked rather than under photos/.
*.rw2

# ...and the same for a cut-out plate source, which is a 20MB RGBA PNG and gets
# dropped in the same place. Root only, by path rather than by extension: the
# repo's other PNGs are design/og/og-source.png and the committed shots, and a
# blanket *.png would take those with it.
/*.png

# the two Texturelabs plates the effect stack is baked from — 9MB and 12MB, and
# handed to design/effects/build-textures.py by path from the repo root, so they
# land here the way an RW2 does. What ships is portfolio/img/tex/, which IS
# committed. There is a licence reason as well as a size one: texturelabs.org
# asks that the source files not be redistributed as textures, and a baked,
# cut-down, blended derivative is a different thing from the original asset.
# Attribution is in portfolio/img/tex/README.md.
/Texturelabs_*.jpg

# ...and the 2x2 lay-up build-textures.py writes beside the paper tile so its
# seams can be looked at rather than taken on trust. A diagnostic, rebuilt on
# every run, and nothing serves it.
portfolio/img/tex/paper-seam-proof.png

# secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*
